KG42.register("rules-2ea24299ea33ad9f11f97d32",{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R015","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R015","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-ancillary-service","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The utility, acting as the community's ancillary-service procurement coordinator, issues incentive signals by broadcasting required service quantities and offered service prices to all community customers. Scope: The power utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community for the Target Time Period T. Condition: Based on assessment of the future operational status of the power system. The published ancillary-service incentive prices are fixed by the utility. Scope: Ancillary-service incentive prices published in Step 1 and used for customer bidding in Step 2.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R015-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"coordination.price_signal","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R015-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Ancillary-service incentive prices published in Step 1 and used for customer bidding in Step 2. | The power utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community for the Target Time Period T.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E10-as-step2-bid-form-eq17","v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"theta-DAS","symbol":"D_t^{AS}","meaning":"Magnitude (kW) of ancillary service required for time slot t, published by the power utility as the set D^{AS} over the Target Time Period T.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"kW","indices":["t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication"]},{"parameter_id":"theta-pAS","symbol":"p_t^{AS}","meaning":"Ancillary-service incentive price (£/kW/h) for time slot t that the power utility is willing to pay, published as the set p^{AS} over the Target Time Period T and fixed for customer bidding.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"£/kW/h","indices":["t ∈ T"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E10-as-step2-bid-form-eq17"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R015-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The utility, acting as the community's ancillary-service procurement coordinator, issues incentive signals by broadcasting required service quantities and offered service prices to all community customers. Scope: The power utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community for the Target Time Period T. Condition: Based on assessment of the future operational status of the power system.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-DAS","theta-pAS"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E23","v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R015-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The published ancillary-service incentive prices are fixed by the utility. Scope: Ancillary-service incentive prices published in Step 1 and used for customer bidding in Step 2.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-pAS"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E10-as-step2-bid-form-eq17"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R015-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The published ancillary-service total-demand and price schedules are defined for the Target Time Period T by D^{AS} = {D_t^{AS} | t ∈ T} (15) and p^{AS} = {p_t^{AS} | t ∈ T} (16), where D_t^{AS} is the required service magnitude for slot t and p_t^{AS} is the offered service price for slot t.","expression":"D^{AS} = \\{D_t^{AS} \\mid t \\in T\\}, \\quad p^{AS} = \\{p_t^{AS} \\mid t \\in T\\}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-DAS","theta-pAS"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R015-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"supporting","statement":"The power utility specifies the type of ancillary services needed, either 'Type-1 AS' or 'Type-2 AS'.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R015-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"exception","statement":"How the power utility decides D^{AS} and p^{AS} involves comprehensive analysis of the power systems managed by the power utility and is out of the scope of this paper; no utility-side optimization for these signals is specified.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["theta-DAS","theta-pAS"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E23","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M03-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"2. Methodological framework ri in In this paper, a framework for ancillary service provision from a ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"After that, in the ancillary service mechanism (shown as the red dashed circle) the power utility will assess its operational needs and issue incentive signals for obtaining ancillary services, and the customers will respond to the signals by submitting bids for providing ancillary services based on the consideration of maximizing their respective economic benefits. The power utility will then assess the bids and make purchase decisions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c1r2__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"of the net load of a customer as a whole, rather than the change of power output/consumption of spec","equation_id":"(15)-(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"As the first step, based on the assessment of the future operational status of power systems, the power utility will broadcast the total demand and prices of ancillary services to all the customers in the P2P energy trading community: \\(D^{AS}=\\{D_t^{AS}\\,|\\,t\\in T\\}\\), (15) \\(p^{AS}=\\{p_t^{AS}\\,|\\,t\\in T\\}\\), (16) where \\(D^{AS}\\) is the set of the magnitude (kW) of the ancillary services required for the time slots within the Target Time Period T, and \\(p^{AS}\\) is the set of prices (£/kW/h) that the power utility is willing to pay for the ancillary services provided by the customers. The power utility will also specify the type of ancillary services needed (either 'Type-1 AS' or 'Type-2 AS'). Note that how the power utility decides \\(D^{AS}\\) and \\(p^{AS}\\) involves comprehensive analysis of the power systems managed by the power utility, which is out of the scope of this paper."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E10-as-step2-bid-form-eq17","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M03-bidding","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"D = Dt |t ∈T , (15) tr { } arpAS = pASt |t ∈T , (16) where DAS is the set of the magnitude (kW) of t","equation_id":"(17)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"After receiving the demand and prices of ancillary services required by the power utility as described in Step 1, the customers will run optimization and submit their bids to the power utility. A bid is in the form of \\(B_i^{AS}=\\{b_{i,t}^{AS}\\,|\\,t\\in T\\}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*\\subseteq I,\\) (17) where \\(B_i^{AS}\\) is the bid of customer i for providing ancillary services for the Target Time Period T, and \\(b_{i,t}^{AS}\\) is the magnitude (kW) of the service that the customer would like to provide for the time slot t. \\(I^*\\) is the set of the customers who submit the bids. Note that the bids only include the amount of services to be provided. In the design of this paper, the prices of the services are fixed by the utility as published in Step 1."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Applied Energy 278 (2020) 115671 ng After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy trading community (a time window can be defined in the Agreement Period for this purpose), the power utility needs to decide which of and to what extent the bids are to be accepted/declined. To achieve the fairness, the power utility in principle should distribute the amount of services to be procured averagely on the customers who have submitted the bids. However, the amount of services to be procured from each customer (called as the 'quota') calculated in this way may be higher than some customers' bids, and thus the surplus quotas can be given to other customers in need. With the above considerations, the process detailed in Fig. 3 is proposed for the power utility to decide the amount of services to be procured from the customers."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design or operational decision variable is modeled in this coordination rule. The only source-supported objects are the utility's published schedules D_t^{AS} and p_t^{AS}, which are fixed signal parameters for customer bidding; E09 explicitly states that how the utility decides D^{AS} and p^{AS} is out of scope.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-bidding","v141-a-M03-clearing","v141-a-M03-participation","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E23","quote":"the power utility will assess its operational needs and issue incentive signals for obtaining ancillary services"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E09-as-step1-publication","quote":"As the first step, based on the assessment of the future operational status of power systems, the power utility will broadcast the total demand and prices of ancillary services to all the customers in the P2P energy trading community:"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","quote":"After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy trading community (a time window can be defined in the Agreement Period for this purpose), the power utility needs to decide which of and to what extent the bids are to be accepted/declined."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E10-as-step2-bid-form-eq17","quote":"In the design of this paper, the prices of the services are fixed by the utility as published in Step 1."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"c35f610ee4a9fa57f1ec958a1d7419f28e1ebf78175d3798b6ba926d42237fd6","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The supplied B evidence explicitly gives the Step-1 ancillary-service publication equations (15)-(16), defining D^{AS} and p^{AS} over T, and states that the service prices are fixed by the utility. The utility's method for choosing these signals is explicitly out of scope, so D_t^{AS} and p_t^{AS} are represented as published parameters rather than modeled decision variables. B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"theta-DAS","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R015-E001"],"rationale":"D_t^{AS} is one of the required service quantities broadcast through the local_operator-to-price_signal coordination edge; the source places the utility's determination out of scope, so it is a published parameter rather than a modeled decision variable."},{"object_id":"theta-pAS","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R015-E001"],"rationale":"p_t^{AS} is the published incentive price broadcast through the local_operator-to-price_signal coordination edge and is fixed by the utility for customer bidding."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R015-C003","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R015-E001"],"rationale":"Equations (15)-(16) define the quantity and price schedules whose publication is represented by the utility's coordination signal on edge E001."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
